menu "ledctl CCT Configuration"

    config LEDCTL_PROV_POP
        string "BLE provisioning proof-of-possession"
        default "abcd1234"
        help
            Shared secret the app must present before the WiFi credential
            exchange proceeds (Security1: X25519 + this PoP + AES-CTR) — see
            docs/04-firmware.md#provisioning-ble. A fixed value baked into
            every device is fine for a private/single-user build; a product
            for other people needs one unique per device (e.g. from a
            manufacturing partition or printed on the enclosure), since
            anyone who knows it can pair with any un-provisioned unit in BLE
            range.

    config LEDCTL_PROV_RESET_GPIO
        int "Provisioning reset button GPIO"
        default 9
        help
            Held low (BOOT button, active-low) for 5s, wipes the stored WiFi
            provisioning and reboots into BLE pairing mode. GPIO9 is the BOOT
            button on most ESP32-C3 dev boards.

    config LEDCTL_DEVICE_NAME
        string "Device name"
        default "ledctl-cct"
        help
            Shown in the app's device list and used as the mDNS instance
            name. Rename per-device once you have more than one.

    config LEDCTL_CCT_MIN_K
        int "Minimum color temperature (K, warmest)"
        default 2700

    config LEDCTL_CCT_MAX_K
        int "Maximum color temperature (K, coldest)"
        default 6500

    config LEDCTL_WARM_GPIO
        int "Warm channel PWM GPIO"
        default 4
        help
            LEDC channel 0. Defaults match docs/06-hardware.md's suggested
            GPIO assignment for a typical ESP32-C3 dev board.

    config LEDCTL_COLD_GPIO
        int "Cold channel PWM GPIO"
        default 5

endmenu
